N2  - Porphyry deposits, due to their significant size and economic value, have long been a focus of research. Nevertheless, the majority of studies concentrate on the genesis of porphyry deposits, with relatively few considering how post-formation preservation conditions go on to influence their present-day distribution. The unique geographical setting of the Tibetan Plateau makes it a key region for investigating the interplay between ore deposits, tectonic deformation, and geomorphic evolution in a
